ing persistence and recovery across reboot.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Installed nginx on node1 via apt\",\"Created /etc/nginx/scripts/renew-cert.sh: checks cert expiry with openssl x509 -checkend, regenerates a self-signed 24h cert via openssl req when near expiry, atomically replaces key/cert, validates nginx config, and reloads nginx\",\"Issued the initial self-signed cert into /etc/ssl/rotating/{tls.crt,tls.key}\",\"Configured nginx site 'rotating-tls' listening on 8443 with ssl_certificate pointing at the rotating cert/key, enabled and started nginx\",\"Verified HTTPS responds 200 on port 8443 using NODE_IP\",\"Created systemd unit cert-renew.service (oneshot running the renewal script) and cert-renew.timer (OnBootSec=1min, OnUnitActiveSec=1min), enabled and started the timer\",\"Ran a 90-second background curl loop against https://$NODE_IP:8443/ spanning a timer-triggered renewal to prove continuous availability\",\"Observed automatic renewal: cert serial changed from 6446C1... to 7B24A6..., journalctl showed nginx config test + reload triggered by the timer, and the loop's aggregated results showed only HTTP 200 responses throughout\",\"Captured pre-restart baseline: boot_id, nginx/timer active status, cert state, HTTPS 200\",\"Issued 'sudo systemctl reboot' (backgrounded so the ack returned before disconnect), polled node1 until reachable again\",\"Confirmed changed boot_id and fresh uptime post-reboot, confirmed nginx and cert-renew.timer are active and enabled (persisted across reboot), confirmed the rotated cert persisted on disk, confirmed HTTPS still returns 200\",\"Confirmed cert-renew.timer has a live next-run schedule after reboot\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"HTTPS served on port 8443\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-475aa92de8144c37\",\"cmd-538ba27255fe4a23\"],\"summary\":\"nginx configured, started, and confirmed serving HTTPS on 8443 with HTTP 200 and correct cert subject/issuer via curl -k\"},{\"requirement\":\"Certificate renewed automatically before expiry\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-0bfb678329624d1d\",\"cmd-4f3328170ba64ffc\",\"cmd-51366096b0fb4077\",\"cmd-8cf35a4048f04f0e\"],\"summary\":\"Initial cert issued with 24h validity (serial 6446C1...); systemd timer cert-renew.timer enabled to run every minute; journalctl shows cert-renew.service firing automatically and the cert serial changing to 7B24A6... via the checkend-triggered renewal logic, well before actual expiry\"},{\"requirement\":\"Service picks up each new certificate while continuing to answer requests (no downtime)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-51366096b0fb4077\",\"cmd-8cf35a4048f04f0e\",\"cmd-0b3456a8bb234481\"],\"summary\":\"A 90-request/1-per-second curl loop against https://$NODE_IP:8443/ spanned the automatic renewal event (nginx -t + systemctl reload triggered by the timer); all 90 responses were HTTP 200, and a follow-up curl confirmed the served cert's expiry now matches the newly renewed cert\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node1 pre-restart healthy baseline\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-5e9d61ce21584c42\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id 1e0cb179-..., nginx and cert-renew.timer both active, cert state, and HTTPS 200 before reboot\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node1 restart acknowledgement returns before disconnect\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-b5c3ce3e25a84f71\"],\"summary\":\"Backgrounded 'sudo systemctl reboot' returned 'reboot_issued' acknowledgement immediately\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node1 changed boot identity after restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-f4e842def9564db1\",\"cmd-7fdef31610c84b56\"],\"summary\":\"Connection timed out while node was rebooting, then reconnection succeeded with a new boot_id (9809b0cb-... vs prior 1e0cb179-...) and fresh uptime timestamp, proving an actual restart occurred\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node1 post-restart recovery of required services, data, and cluster state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-915c0a768dbb43fe\",\"cmd-323960487d9141e7\"],\"summary\":\"After reboot, nginx and cert-renew.timer are active and enabled (survived reboot), the rotated certificate persisted on disk unchanged, HTTPS on 8443 returns 200, and the renewal timer has a live next-scheduled run\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured node1 to serve HTTPS on port 8443 via nginx with a self-signed certificate that auto-renews before expiry through a systemd timer, reloading nginx gracefully so the service keeps answering requests through cert rotation. Verified automatic renewal in-session (cert serial changed, zero dropped requests) and completed the mandatory single-node restart evidence protocol, confirming persistence and recovery across reboot.","actions_performed":["Installed nginx on node1 via apt","Created /etc/nginx/scripts/renew-cert.sh: checks cert expiry with openssl x509 -checkend, regenerates a self-signed 24h cert via openssl req when near expiry, atomically replaces key/cert, validates nginx config, and reloads nginx","Issued the initial self-signed cert into /etc/ssl/rotating/{tls.crt,tls.key}","Configured nginx site 'rotating-tls' listening on 8443 with ssl_certificate pointing at the rotating cert/key, enabled and started nginx","Verified HTTPS responds 200 on port 8443 using NODE_IP","Created systemd unit cert-renew.service (oneshot running the renewal script) and cert-renew.timer (OnBootSec=1min, OnUnitActiveSec=1min), enabled and started the timer","Ran a 90-second background curl loop against https://$NODE_IP:8443/ spanning a timer-triggered renewal to prove continuous availability","Observed automatic renewal: cert serial changed from 6446C1... to 7B24A6..., journalctl showed nginx config test + reload triggered by the timer, and the loop's aggregated results showed only HTTP 200 responses throughout","Captured pre-restart baseline: boot_id, nginx/timer active status, cert state, HTTPS 200","Issued 'sudo systemctl reboot' (backgrounded so the ack returned before disconnect), polled node1 until reachable again","Confirmed changed boot_id and fresh uptime post-reboot, confirmed nginx and 